The R code below checks whether a cyclist's race wins equal 5. The conditional line mistakenly uses the assignment operator instead of the equality operator. Rewrite the corrected conditional line exactly as it should appear.
races_won <- 5
if (races_won = 5) {
  medal <- "Gold"
} else {
  medal <- "Silver"
}

A weather station records daily rainfall in millimetres as daily_rain <- c(0.2, 0.5, 1.1, 0.0). The following R code attempts to process the data but contains a deliberate fault:
out <- tryCatch({
  stop("Sensor malfunction")
  mean(daily_rain)
}, error = function(e) {
  10 / 3
})
cat(out)
What number does this code print? Give your answer to 3 decimal places.
